netflix's the silent sea ended on one  heck of a cliffhanger what's going to  happen to luna will the truth of the  balhe station come to light this is the  end of the silent sea explained  so what really happens in the final  moments of the first season the final  episode of the silent sea ends with a  rescue ship arriving with the intent of  heading back to earth but not much else  is known for certain including the  health of sung hong and luna everyone  else from the mission dies in one way or  another with the two doctors and the  child being the only survivors even han  who seems so close to surviving  sacrifices himself in the final moments  so that the others can escape with luna  as for the lunar water they have some  samples but there's no way anyone else  can get more as ball hey station is  completely destroyed by the water itself  this gets rid of one problem for soon as  it means that rx and other organizations  won't try to retrieve more samples but  they still don't even know how the water  was found in the first place but with  luna and a few samples soon hung and  other like-minded researchers could  potentially discover the answers for  themselves  for people like captain han director  choi and ryu their desperation to find  an answer is simply to improve their own  status they need lunar water to be the  thing that saves everyone just as soon's  sister did in the case of sung and hong  the two doctors who represent the other  end of the spectrum they believe in the  mission to appoint but they also know  there's no miracle cure to the world  water crisis and from the beginning they  are clear about their value of human  life soon and hong know to ask whether  it is really worth it especially after  witnessing firsthand how brutal and  deadly lunar water really is while soon  would love for the water to be the  ultimate cure she isn't willing to  sacrifice the lives of those around her  just for some dream  throughout season one captain han shares  the same pragmatic logical understanding  as soon but he has his daughter to fight  for so he's willing to do almost  anything to complete the mission but  then enters luna a super-powered little  girl who is desperate to keep the lunar  water to herself soon sees through the  violence and realizes that it's not a  monster attacking them but a girl who  can survive the water through further  investigation it's discovered that the  balje crew were experimenting with the  water on numbered clones known as luna  each time the girls died until number 73  which is the luna the crew meets upon  their arrival even after discovering all  of this han still has one goal and  that's finding the samples and bringing  them back to earth even if that means  killing luna but once they meet face to  face luna is the final straw for han  bringing him to his senses about what's  really important she reminds him of his  daughter who looks to be around the same  age and desperately needs water to  survive the entire reason he goes on the  mission is for his daughter but luna  reminds him that there are other  children and other people that matter  just as much while the water sample is  still a major priority luna's survival  and the hope that she can live a real  life is the true mission  there are plenty of unanswered questions  at the end of the silent sea season one  the two biggest mysteries are luna and  lunar water as there's still not a lot  known about either in the penultimate  episode ryu insinuates to han that  there's much more about the original  mission and the lunar water itself that  they don't know saying  you don't know anything  nothing  about what happened  he's right for example if they were  finding success with luna 73 what really  led troy to shut down the study of  course there's also everything about  luna that we don't know while she can  clearly survive the lunar water it  doesn't just sustain her but it also  gives her advanced healing speed  strength eyesight and probably a lot  more oh and she can also survive in the  moon's atmosphere so how does all this  happen we see the experiments that led  to luna 73 but not much else about her  background as for her connection to the  water luna's bite allows soon to survive  the water's infection but what else  might it do  although the silent sea season one ends  with only a few of the original crew  left standing and a rescue ship arriving  the events after that are unclear early  on in episode 8 soon declares her plan  for luna and herself stating that she  will escort them both to the  international institute of space biology  the show provides a short look at the  iisb though nothing else about it is  revealed as soon states that they can't  bring the sample or luna back to earth  we can assume that she enacts a plan to  get to the iisb which would likely be  explored in season 2. even though it  portrays itself as neutral territory  there will probably be trouble there as  well also there's no way choi or rx are  letting this resource go without a fight  there's also the question of whether or  not to reveal the truth about baal hey  station which is brought up earlier in  the final episode both hong and soon  want to expose the truth of what  happened on the station but this would  likely have huge ramifications for  everyone if a second season does come to  netflix we can expect this plot thread  to be further explored check out one of  our newest videos right here plus even  more looper videos about your favorite  netflix originals are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]
 

